1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,410
Penny walks into a casino with one hundred dollars.

2
00:00:03,730 --> 00:00:06,759
She never bets more than a dollar at a time.

3
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:13,099
But by the time that hundred is gone, she'll have bet, on average, almost fourteen hundred dollars.

4
00:00:13,419 --> 00:00:16,230
And the casino never had to cheat her once.

5
00:00:16,879 --> 00:00:20,769
Last episode, Costco sold Penny the feeling of belonging.

6
00:00:21,089 --> 00:00:23,780
Casinos sell her something stranger:

7
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:26,059
the feeling that she might win.

8
00:00:26,379 --> 00:00:32,159
Here are the three engines that turn that feeling into seventy-eight billion dollars a year.

9
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:34,539
Engine number one:

10
00:00:34,859 --> 00:00:37,759
the edge. Take American roulette.

11
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:40,359
The wheel has thirty-eight pockets.

12
00:00:40,679 --> 00:00:43,750
Thirty-six numbers, plus two green zeros.

13
00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:49,359
Bet a dollar on one number and win, and the casino pays you thirty-five dollars.

14
00:00:50,009 --> 00:00:52,450
Sounds fair. It isn't.

15
00:00:52,770 --> 00:00:55,329
Fair odds would pay thirty-seven.

16
00:00:55,649 --> 00:01:00,420
So spin it thirty-eight times, win once, and you're still two dollars down.

17
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:05,650
That's about five cents of every dollar you bet, gone, on average, forever.

18
00:01:05,969 --> 00:01:08,790
Every game in the building is built this way.

19
00:01:09,109 --> 00:01:11,239
Blackjack, craps, baccarat.

20
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:15,269
The edge can be tiny, but it always points the same way.

21
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:18,439
And sometimes, it's not so tiny.

22
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:28,680
Some wheels have just one green zero, and that one extra pocket nearly doubles the casino's cut, from under three cents a dollar to over five.

23
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,469
Same wheel. Same game.

24
00:01:31,790 --> 00:01:33,030
Twice the edge.

25
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:36,750
Engine number two is where the real money is:

26
00:01:37,069 --> 00:01:38,400
slot machines.

27
00:01:38,719 --> 00:01:44,329
In Nevada, slots brought in about ten and a half billion dollars in twenty twenty-four.

28
00:01:44,650 --> 00:01:48,719
That's roughly two thirds of everything the state's casinos won.

29
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:54,200
And on average, Nevada's slots kept about seven cents of every dollar played.

30
00:01:54,849 --> 00:01:56,879
Seven cents sounds small.

31
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,590
But here's the trick.

32
00:01:58,909 --> 00:02:01,549
When Penny wins, she doesn't walk away.

33
00:02:01,870 --> 00:02:03,810
She puts the winnings back in.

34
00:02:04,129 --> 00:02:10,340
The same money goes round and round, and the machine takes its little slice every single time.

35
00:02:10,659 --> 00:02:18,020
That's how one hundred dollars turns into almost fourteen hundred dollars of bets, until the casino has all of it.

36
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:20,090
It's not one big loss.

37
00:02:20,409 --> 00:02:23,629
It's a thousand tiny ones that feel like a game.

38
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:27,310
And now, the machine doesn't even need a building.

39
00:02:27,629 --> 00:02:39,340
Last year, Americans lost almost seventeen billion dollars to sportsbooks, and almost eleven billion to online casino games, both growing by more than a fifth in a single year.

40
00:02:39,659 --> 00:02:43,629
The slot machine is now in Penny's pocket, open all night.

41
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:46,050
Engine number three:

42
00:02:46,370 --> 00:02:48,849
the freebies. Free drinks.

43
00:02:49,169 --> 00:02:51,770
Free rooms. Free buffets.

44
00:02:52,090 --> 00:02:54,629
Casinos hand out a lot for free.

45
00:02:54,949 --> 00:03:00,370
But that loyalty card Penny swipes tracks how much she bets and how long she plays.

46
00:03:00,689 --> 00:03:07,830
The casino knows its edge, so it can work out roughly how much she'll lose, and hand a slice of that back as gifts.

47
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:11,020
Those freebies aren't generosity.

48
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:17,740
They're a rebate on her own losses, designed to keep her playing longer, and to bring her back next month.

49
00:03:18,389 --> 00:03:20,099
So here's the machine.

50
00:03:20,419 --> 00:03:24,069
The edge makes sure the casino wins over enough bets.

51
00:03:24,389 --> 00:03:27,080
The churn makes sure you place enough bets.

52
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:30,719
And the freebies make sure you come back to place more.

53
00:03:31,039 --> 00:03:33,860
The casino doesn't need you to lose big.

54
00:03:34,180 --> 00:03:36,360
It just needs you to keep playing.

55
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:41,430
So if you gamble, treat it like a ticket to a show, not a way to make money.

56
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:47,090
One: decide your budget before you walk in, and leave your cards at home.

57
00:03:47,409 --> 00:03:50,479
Two: when you win, walk away with it.

58
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,229
Don't feed it back.

59
00:03:52,550 --> 00:03:58,370
Three: skip the games with the biggest edge, like keno and double-zero roulette.

60
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:01,409
Casinos don't win by luck.

61
00:04:01,729 --> 00:04:05,099
They win by math, repeated millions of times.

62
00:04:05,419 --> 00:04:10,409
But some of the biggest money machines in the world don't charge you anything at all.

63
00:04:10,729 --> 00:04:14,319
How free apps make billions, next on Money Mechanics.

